  "name": "eventually-rs",
  "description": "A comprehensive toolkit for building event-sourced systems in Rust, emphasizing Domain-Driven Design principles such as Aggregate Roots and Bounded Contexts. It provides a robust set of traits for command handling, event persistence, and state folding, featuring a production-ready PostgreSQL backend with built-in optimistic concurrency control. The framework simplifies the implementation of complex domain logic through specialized procedural macros and provides integration paths for gRPC and Protobuf-based microservices.",
